"Careful" is not the same thing as "never bring it up."

I'm always surprised to find that most people's lists have little to do with 
actual spelling. It's easier for me to remember keys that are the first 
initial of what I'm using. I generally only adjust letters for worn items 
and tools, since they're the only things I'll be using often enough that 
looking at an inventory list gets annoying.

A - Armor      /* Capital letters here because they're used with *
B - Boots       * the "W" and "T" commands; just hold down the   *
C - Cloak       * shift key                                      */ 
G - Gloves (or Gauntlets)
H - Helmet
R - Robe
S - Shield
T - T-shirt or Hawaiian Shirt

t - towel or blindfold  /* "B" and "b" are used for other things. */

b - bag (sack or BoH)            
c - expensive camara              
k - key, lockpick, or credit card  /* No point in having different 
l - lamp (any light source)         * letters for the same function */
s - stethoscope

That's pretty much it. Used to use "d" for daggers or darts, but now I just 
"Q"uiver whatever it is I want to throw. Sometimes use "a" for my primary 
weapon, but if I'm only using one I don't need to bother with the inventory 
letter; if I'm swapping back and forth between two, I have the second 
readied as a secondary weapon and just use "x" to swap them. Sometimes 
designate artifact weapons by first initial if it seems helpful; sometimes 
use "X", "Y", and "Z" for invocation artifacts, since you can't bag them and 
they have to stay in main inventory (unless you stash them, which I never 
do)--keeps them out of the way.

